WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.367
-Pierce, looking fantastic
as always, buddy.

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:05.067
Look at you on the cover
of "GQ" magazine

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:07.267
right here, by the way.
-Yeah, that's sweet.

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.567
-Yeah, I mean, come on.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:11.767
-It's the boys inside, though.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:13.901
Those are the ones, my boys.
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.167
-Yes.
-They're inside, as well.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:17.033
But, look --
come on, let's go back to you.

00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:18.567
-Thank you.
-Tonight is about you.

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:20.734
What is it like
to be so good-looking?

00:00:20.734 --> 00:00:22.267
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:24.534
-Let's get to the -- let's get
to the hard-hitting question.

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.400
-Yeah, well,
long may it last, Jimmy.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.033
Long may it last.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:29.701
-So far, so good.
How you keeping?

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:31.901
You're looking all grown up now
with your beard.

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:34.200
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.000
Jimmy with a beard.
-Yeah, thank you very much.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.133
-It's cool, man.
-It is cool.

00:00:37.133 --> 00:00:38.667
-It's majestic.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:41.100
-It's majestic.
You're the greatest, come on.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.334
-It is, man.
-I love having you on.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:45.133
I love talking about your
painting, by the way.

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:46.601
You know I'm a big fan of
your paint -- your paintings.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.501
-Thanks.
Appreciate it.

00:00:48.501 --> 00:00:49.701
-They're gorgeous.
And you're actually

00:00:49.701 --> 00:00:50.968
about to have your first show.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:53.701
-May 13th.
That's it, next year.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:56.734
I've postponed this
so many times because of work,

00:00:56.734 --> 00:00:58.868
and so, finally, I've said,
"Whatever movie I'm doing,

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.267
I'm going to do the show."

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.300
Santa Monica, May 13th.

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.534
-You're doing it.
-I'm doing it.

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:05.367
-Are you nervous?
-Well, not now,

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:07.734
but I will be then, probably,
you know when --

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.934
-How many years
have you been painting?

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:12.434
-Since, I'd say, '87.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:14.501
-1987.
I mean, I'm self-taught.

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:16.567
-You're so talented.
We want to show a couple,

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:18.234
just so we can see --
-Yeah, go ahead, man.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:19.234
Go ahead.
-This one I --

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:20.801
This one I actually love.

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:23.334
I wish --
This one's called "Ear Plugs."

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:25.334
-Yep, painted.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:25.334 --> 00:01:27.701
It's original.
-I don't know why

00:01:27.701 --> 00:01:29.834
we started with this one,
but I do enjoy this one.

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:31.467
I really do like this.
-It is.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:33.567
It's really nice.
I'm a big Lichtenstein --

00:01:33.567 --> 00:01:35.000
Roy Lichtenstein,
a great artist.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.467
-Yes.
-I'm a big fan of his work.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:39.667
And I painted it
when I was doing "Goldeneye"

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:40.868
down at Leavesden Studios.

00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:42.467
-Yeah.
That's what I'm talking about.

00:01:42.467 --> 00:01:43.701
-There you go.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:45.968
-Did you used to have --
I'm assuming --

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:48.100
[ Applause ]

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.934
I'm assuming you'd have
to wear ear plugs

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.834
for a lot of the scenes.
-Well, yeah, of course.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:53.133
I mean, you have to --
they give you these

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:55.200
little packets every time
there's explosions.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.834
And so, I thought
I'd just paint it.

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:58.667
So, over six months,
I painted that.

00:01:58.667 --> 00:02:00.067
-You made it into a work of art.
I love that.

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:01.767
-That's it.

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:04.901
-This one is "Picasso."
-"Picasso."

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:06.901
He is --
you know, he influences me.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:08.133
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
I'm very...

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:10.334
-I know, right?
-...appreciative of his work.

00:02:10.334 --> 00:02:12.400
He's a great inspiration.
He is -- you know,

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:16.234
it all begins and starts
and ends with Pablo.

00:02:16.234 --> 00:02:19.334
-What got you into art?

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:20.767
-I -- I --
Oh, God.

00:02:20.767 --> 00:02:22.601
-Do you remember your first
time, you go like, "Oh, wow."

00:02:22.601 --> 00:02:26.334
'Cause I --
-Well, I left school at 16, 17,

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:28.367
with nothing but
a cardboard folder

00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:30.100
of drawings and paintings.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:33.200
Got a job in a little studio
in Putney, South London,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.267
and I thought,
"I'm off to be an artist."

00:02:35.267 --> 00:02:38.934
And then I discovered acting,
or acting discovered me.

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:40.100
-Yeah, exactly.
-You know?

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:41.400
-Thank God
you made those choices.

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:42.901
-Thank God for that.
-No. We're so happy.

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.801
We love that. I mean,
congrats on the art show.

00:02:44.801 --> 00:02:45.834
-Thanks.
-But, I mean,

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:47.067
you're Pierce Brosnan.

00:02:47.067 --> 00:02:48.501
I mean, you've kind of
done everything, buddy.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.667
It's fantastic.

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:51.234
-Well, it's work in progress,
Jimmy.

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:52.400
-Yeah.
-You know, it really is.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:53.634
You know what it's like.
-But now --

00:02:53.634 --> 00:02:55.667
Now you're a superhero.
-Now I'm a superhero.

00:02:55.667 --> 00:02:56.834
I didn't expect this.
-Now you've actually

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.267
done everything.
You really have.

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:00.901
I mean, this is fantastic.
-Yeah. I really was --

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:04.067
It was the last thing on my mind
to be playing a superhero

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:07.000
like Doctor Fate.
-Doctor Fate.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.534
What a cool superhero.
I mean, did you ever think,

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.734
like, "Oh, yeah,
I would do these --

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.400
I would do a superhero movie?"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:18.234
-No.
-If the right one came along?

00:03:18.234 --> 00:03:19.400
-You would do one?

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.133
-Oh, no,
I would never do one, no.

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.701
No one would offer me one.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:25.133
But, I --
That's not an option for me.

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:28.100
For you, I'm assuming everyone
offered you a bunch of things,

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.501
and you're like, "Well, hold on,
I'm not ready to do this."

00:03:29.501 --> 00:03:32.400
-No, not really. No.
I mean, I went up for Batman

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:35.934
way back in the day
when Tim Burton was doing it.

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:38.067
-Oh, really?
-Obviously I didn't get the job.

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.501
But...
-Yeah.

00:03:39.501 --> 00:03:41.567
You had to settle for
James Bond, sorry, yeah.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:43.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:45.133
I'm so sorry, yeah.

00:03:45.133 --> 00:03:46.934
-I remember saying something
stupid to Tim Burton.

00:03:46.934 --> 00:03:48.801
Like, I said -- I said,
"You know, I can't understand

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.267
any man who would
wear his underpants

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:52.067
outside his trousers."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:52.067 --> 00:03:53.801
And so, it's just like --
-That is very interesting.

00:03:53.801 --> 00:03:55.567
Yes.
-But there you go.

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:58.667
The best man got the job, and,
you know, Doctor Fate and I

00:03:58.667 --> 00:04:00.968
were meant to meet
on the same page, I think.

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:03.901
-This is you as archaeologist,
Kent Nelson, right?

00:04:03.901 --> 00:04:05.868
-Mm-hmm.
-And then, when you put on

00:04:05.868 --> 00:04:10.534
the golden Helmet of Fate,
you become Doctor Fate.

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:15.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:19.167
My question is,
when you're wearing this,

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:21.367
and you can be honest with me,
can you see anything?

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:22.467
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.467 --> 00:04:23.868
No.
-Nothing at all?

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:26.234
-Everybody wants to know what it
was like putting on the costume.

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:27.868
What was it like
putting on the helmet?

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:30.200
You know, you can't see a thing.
It's darkness.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:32.434
I mean, there were two helmets.

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:35.667
There was this stylish,
gorgeous-looking, sleek helmet

00:04:35.667 --> 00:04:37.400
that's in the other photograph.
-Yeah.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:38.567
-And then there was one
that I could actually

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:41.367
physically put on.
But, of course,

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:43.934
you're standing there
in a mocap suit --

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:47.834
a motion-capture suit, which is
the most inelegant and kind of

00:04:47.834 --> 00:04:49.367
humorous thing to wear.
-Yeah.

00:04:49.367 --> 00:04:52.467
Ping-pong balls everywhere.
-ping-pong balls, grey tights,

00:04:52.467 --> 00:04:53.934
you know, you got to have
a sense of humor.

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:56.167
And I won't say it.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.000
-Yep, of course.
We said it for you.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:59.334
Yeah, don't worry about it.
Yeah, we're all good.

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.701
-But I remember
Jaume Collet-Serra,

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:03.501
the director, he said --
There was a point

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:06.267
where I had to find this crown,
and he said --

00:05:06.267 --> 00:05:08.067
I'm standing there,
and I'm giving it my best

00:05:08.067 --> 00:05:10.667
heroic acting, and he said,
"Okay, put the helmet on."

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:12.634
I said, "Don't worry.
I can see it. It's right there."

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:15.334
I put it on. Of course,
I couldn't see anything.

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:17.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:17.133 --> 00:05:19.467
-"We can't CGI that.
Yeah, go ahead.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.334
Just wait.
Try one more take. Yeah."

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:22.868
-Anyway, it was good fun to do.

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:24.367
It was a lovely company
of actors.

00:05:24.367 --> 00:05:26.167
I know you had
Noah on last night.

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:28.000
-Yeah. Dwayne Johnson's
coming on tomorrow.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.934
-Dwayne is coming on.
Oh, good.

00:05:29.934 --> 00:05:32.400
-I mean,
he's one of the greatest,

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:34.067
nicest guys you'll ever meet.
-Yeah.

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.133
-And to have such
a big following and such a --

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:38.467
being such a big star,
he's pretty humble, you know?

00:05:38.467 --> 00:05:39.968
-He is.
-Which I do like.

00:05:39.968 --> 00:05:42.701
Did you get that vibe from him?
-Oh, very much so.

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:44.367
We got on --
I mean, I got to know him more,

00:05:44.367 --> 00:05:46.801
you know, on the press tour
than I did on the movie.

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:50.067
I mean, we had interaction
on the film set,

00:05:50.067 --> 00:05:52.334
but he's a magnificent fellow.

00:05:52.334 --> 00:05:56.267
He's kind of monolithic and
beautiful and owns this role.

00:05:56.267 --> 00:05:57.634
-He is.
-Oh, he is.

00:05:57.634 --> 00:06:00.434
-Yeah.
I'm just happy that you're

00:06:00.434 --> 00:06:02.567
playing a superhero
in a giant, big thing,

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:04.267
'cause you know
I'm the biggest fan of you.

00:06:04.267 --> 00:06:05.534
And we've talked about
everything.

00:06:05.534 --> 00:06:07.534
But, now, you can go,
"Yeah, I've kind of

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:10.100
done it all now, yeah."
And this is the first of many.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.534
'Cause I could see --
I could see where this --

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:13.634
-Well, slow and steady.
-Slow and steady wins the race.

00:06:13.634 --> 00:06:15.133
-Slow and steady.
Yeah.

00:06:15.133 --> 00:06:16.167
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:17.601
Here's Pierce Brosnan
in "Black Adam."

00:06:17.601 --> 00:06:19.033
Take a look at this.

00:06:19.033 --> 00:06:20.667
♪♪

00:06:20.667 --> 00:06:23.000
-A wise man once told me
a bad plan

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.601
is better than no plan at all.

00:06:24.601 --> 00:06:27.934
-That was before
we had a very bad plan.

00:06:27.934 --> 00:06:30.000
-Let it go.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.701
-I'd rather be fighting with him
than against him.

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:35.267
-What's the helmet telling you?

00:06:35.267 --> 00:06:38.000
Somebody's gonna die.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.167
Who is it?
Atom Smasher?

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:40.634
It's Atom Smasher.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:43.033
-Surprisingly, no.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:45.200
-Is it me?

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:49.000
-When it's time for you and I
to say goodbye, you'll know.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.501
♪♪

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:55.067
All I can tell you is,

00:06:55.067 --> 00:06:59.067
there's still time
to change the future.

00:06:59.067 --> 00:07:00.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:00.234 --> 00:07:02.067
-Yes!

00:07:02.067 --> 00:07:03.767
People will be cheering
in the crowd!

00:07:03.767 --> 00:07:05.234
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:07:05.234 --> 00:07:07.234
Pierce Brosnan, everyone!
-Go see it.

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:11.300
-"Black Adam" opens in theaters
and IMAX October 21st.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:12.968
We're talking with Charlie Puth
when we come back.

00:07:12.968 --> 00:07:14.467
Stick around, everybody.

